<title>DENMARK: Danish police foil protest at Dutch embassy.</title>
<headline>Danish police foil protest at Dutch embassy.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish police stopped anti-EU demonstrators from attacking the Dutch embassy overnight, an embassy official said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;We know they were on their way to the embassy because of the leaflets they were carrying,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>The pamphlets referred to a revenge protest at the mission and to the arrest of Danish protesters at the European Union summit in Amsterdam, he said.</p>
<p>The official said police arrested 17 radicals, carrying paint, stones and the protest leaflets, before they could reach the city centre embassy.</p>
</text>
